WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.970
In 1970, world trade was
25.8 per cent of world GDP.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.590
By 2008, it was 60.3 per cent.

3
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.270
Then the long rise stopped.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.270
In 2024 the share was 56.7 per cent.

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.510
Some call this slowbalization.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.410
Meanwhile, in 2016, the UK voted
to leave the European Union.

7
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.110
From 2018, the USA and China raised
tariffs on each other's goods.

8
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.150
Is globalization creating
its own backlash?

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.750
Or are the two simply unrelated?

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.290
In this mission, you'll separate
nationalism from tribalization,

11
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.110
and a correlation from a cause.

12
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.870
Then you'll examine the UK's
2016 vote nation by nation,

13
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.850
and the tariff conflict
between the USA and China.

14
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.710
Your mission: evaluate whether
globalization is creating its own backlash.
